      "explanation": "<p>All the given compounds are acid derivatives, thus contain carbonyl group in them. LiAlH<sub>4</sub> reduces these compounds through nucleophilic substitution via addition elimination (S<sub>N<sub>A</sub></sub>E) reaction. The rate of reaction depends upon the following factors:</p>\n<p>(i) Size of alkyl group.</p>\n<p>(ii) Steric hinderance around the &gt; C == O group.</p>\n<p>(iii) (+) ve charge on the C-atom of &gt; C == O group.</p>\n<p>The alkyl groups are more or less same in the given compounds. Thus, the reactivity order of given compounds depends upon 2nd and 3rd factor written above. The cumulative effect of these two factors results to leaving group ability (LGA) of the substituents in the following order :</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3wn31ul/ce7a0251-d395-4380-8126-520710724ae9/9fb3dcd0-e23d-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wn31um.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l3wn31ul/ce7a0251-d395-4380-8126-520710724ae9/9fb3dcd0-e23d-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wn31um.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2019 (Online) 12th January Evening Slot Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 216 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l3wn31ul/ce7a0251-d395-4380-8126-520710724ae9/9fb3dcd0-e23d-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wn31um.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l3wn31ul/ce7a0251-d395-4380-8126-520710724ae9/9fb3dcd0-e23d-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wn31um.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3wn31ul/ce7a0251-d395-4380-8126-520710724ae9/9fb3dcd0-e23d-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wn31um.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l3wn31ul/ce7a0251-d395-4380-8126-520710724ae9/9fb3dcd0-e23d-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wn31um.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l3wn31ul/ce7a0251-d395-4380-8126-520710724ae9/9fb3dcd0-e23d-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wn31um.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l3wn31ul/ce7a0251-d395-4380-8126-520710724ae9/9fb3dcd0-e23d-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wn31um.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>This leaving group ability (weak conjugate base) corresponds directly to the reactivity order.</p>\n<p>Hence, the correct reactivity order is:</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3wn1d88/b5fc8db8-45f7-4677-b78a-8f451dde933d/70dfa470-e23d-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wn1d89.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l3wn1d88/b5fc8db8-45f7-4677-b78a-8f451dde933d/70dfa470-e23d-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wn1d89.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2019 (Online) 12th January Evening Slot Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 216 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l3wn1d88/b5fc8db8-45f7-4677-b78a-8f451dde933d/70dfa470-e23d-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wn1d89.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l3wn1d88/b5fc8db8-45f7-4677-b78a-8f451dde933d/70dfa470-e23d-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wn1d89.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3wn1d88/b5fc8db8-45f7-4677-b78a-8f451dde933d/70dfa470-e23d-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wn1d89.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l3wn1d88/b5fc8db8-45f7-4677-b78a-8f451dde933d/70dfa470-e23d-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wn1d89.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l3wn1d88/b5fc8db8-45f7-4677-b78a-8f451dde933d/70dfa470-e23d-11ec-9020-b7d4d